  "source_behavior": {
    "ros2-joint-trajectory-controller": {
      "entrypoint": "pluginlib joint_trajectory_controller/JointTrajectoryController (controller_interface::ControllerInterface)",
      "effects": "The selected update reads joint states, samples the companion Trajectory implementation, checks configured tolerances and writes position, velocity, acceleration or effort commands according to selected interfaces. Velocity-only or effort-only configurations can use the PID/feedforward adapter. Configuration creates ~/joint_trajectory input, ~/controller_state output, follow_joint_trajectory action, query_state service and conditional speed-scaling input. It handles goal preemption/cancellation and configured hold/deceleration paths; stopping safety and real-time performance were not tested. Companion trajectory.cpp, headers, generated parameter YAML/validators and their behavior are required but were not reviewed. lifecycle_msgs is explicitly included in this source; the other listed build/runtime dependencies come from package.xml/CMake. Optional BUILD_TESTING has additional declared test dependencies. CMake requests C++17; package 4.43.0 and the jazzy checkout are declarations, not tested ROS, OS, architecture, controller or robot combinations."
    },
    "ros2-diff-drive-controller": {
      "entrypoint": "pluginlib diff_drive_controller/DiffDriveController (controller_interface::ChainableControllerInterface)",
      "effects": "The subscriber path uses the package TwistStamped alias on ~/cmd_vel and checks timestamp age; timeout 0 disables this timeout. The chainable class exposes linear/angular velocity reference interfaces. update_and_write_commands applies speed limiters, computes wheel rates from linear x/angular z and configured geometry, and writes loaned wheel command handles. It delegates odometry to odometry.cpp, publishes ~/odom and conditional /tf and ~/cmd_vel_out, and halt writes zero wheel commands during deactivation. These are source operations, not verified stopping, odometry accuracy or timing. Complete headers, odometry/speed-limiter helpers and generated parameter YAML/validators were not reviewed and remain required. Package/CMake declare the listed build/runtime dependencies; lifecycle_msgs, class_loader and rosidl_runtime_cpp also appear directly in this source. Optional BUILD_TESTING has additional declared test dependencies. C++17, package 4.43.0 and the jazzy checkout are declarations, not tested environment combinations."
    }
  },
